                                                  \n                                            \n                \n                \n                \n            \n            \n\n        \n                        \n        \n                                                                                            \n                        \n\n        \n        \n                                                                \n                        \n                        \n                                    \n        \n                \n                    \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \n                                                                                    \n                    \n                        \n    \n    \n    \n        \n    \n\n    \n        \n                        \n        \n        \n                        \n\n                                                                        \n                                    \n        \n                                                \n                                                                                                        \n                        \n                                    \n        \n                \n                    \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \n                                                                                    \n                    \n                        \n    \n    \n    \n        \n    \n\n    \n        \n                        \n        \n        \n                        \n\n        \n        \n        \n                \n                    \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \n                                                \n                    \n                        \n    \n    \n    \n        \n    \n\n    \n        \n                        \n        \n        \n                        \n\n        \n        \n                                                                                                \n        \n                \n                    \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \n                                                \n                    \n                        \n    \n    \n    \n        \n    \n\n    \n        \n                        \n        \n        \n                        \n\n        \n        \n                                                \n                        \n                        \n                                    \n        \n                \n                    \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \n                                                                                    \n                    \n                        \n    \n    \n    \n        \n    \n\n    \n        \n                        \n        \n        \n                        \n\n        \n        \n                                                \n                        \n                        \n                                    \n        \n                \n                    \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \n                                                                                    \n                    \n                        \n    \n    \n    \n        \n    \n\n    \n        \n                        \n        \n        \n                        \n\n        \n        \n                                                \n                        \n                        \n                                    \n        \n                \n                    \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \n                                                                                    \n                    \n                        \n    \n    \n    \n        \n    \n\n    \n        \n                        \n        \n        \n                        \n\n        \n        \n                                                                                                                                    \n        \n                \n                    \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \n                                                \n                    \n                        \n    \n    \n    \n        \n    \n\n    \n        \n                        \n        \n        \n                        \n\n        \n        \n                                                \n                        \n                        \n                                    \n        \n                \n                    \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \n                                                                                                                                                                \n                    \n                        \n    \n    \n    \n        \n    \n\n    \n        \n                        \n        \n        \n                        \n\n        \n        \n                                                \n                        \n                        \n                                    \n        \n                \n                    \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \n                                                                                    \n                    \n                        \n    \n    \n    \n        \n    \n\n    \n        \n                        \n        \n        \n                        \n\n        \n        \n                                                \n                        \n                        \n                                    \n        \n                \n                    \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \n                                                                                    \n                    \n                    \n    \n    \n        \n                \n                    \n                                    \n\n\n\t\t\n\n\n\n\n                                        <!-- No AdsNinja v10 Client! --><!-- No AdsNinja v10 Client! --><!-- No AdsNinja v10 Client! --><!-- No AdsNinja v10 Client! -->\n\n                \n<div itemprop=\"articleBody\" id=\"article-body\"><p>Canva has helped countless people pursue their passion in graphic design with absolutely no training in it. Since its creation, there has not really been much competition when it comes to a platform that can be used by virtually anyone to create professional-looking graphics and presentations of all kinds. </p>    <!-- No AdsNinja v10 Client! --><!-- No AdsNinja v10 Client! --><p>Google is looking to change that with Google Pics, which is both a standalone app and an integration in Google Workspace. It was announced at Google I/O 2026 back in May, but just became widely available today.</p>    \n    \n    \n    \n<!-- No AdsNinja v10 Client! --><h2 id=\"how-it-works\">\n                        How it works\n               </h2>\n<p>Google Pics, unsurprisingly, uses AI to generate images and designs. You can create new images with a prompt or you can build on pre-existing elements by uploading and modifying images from Google Drive, Photos, or your local device.</p>    <p>While Google Pics does not offer the design freedom of Canva, where AI is optional, it has object segmentation and does allow for some tweaking so that you can edit, move, or resize specific parts of the designs it generates. As Google puts it, “no more ‘prompt-and-pray.’”</p>    <p>Text can be translated right within the design, which lets you expand your project across multiple languages easily. </p>    <!-- No AdsNinja v10 Client! --><h2 id=\"how-to-access-it\">\n                        How to access it\n               </h2>\n<p>You can try out Google Pics at <a href=\"https://workspace.google.com/products/pics/\" target=\"_blank\">pics.new</a>. </p>    \n\n                \n<p>It’s rolling out over the next few weeks. It is available for Workspace customers with Business Standard, Business Plus, Enterprise Standard, and Enterprise Plus plans; Google AI Pro for Education users; as well as Google AI Pro and Ultra subscribers. </p>    <p>It will be a standalone product, and also integrated with Google Drive and Slides at its start and will eventually be in Google Docs as well. </p>    </div>\n    \n            \n                        \n                \n        \n        \n\n                    \n    \n                        \n    \n\n\n            \n                                \n        \n        \n    \n\n        \n    </article>\n\n    \n            \n        </DIV></DIV>","content_text":"Published Sep 1, 2026, 3:43 PM EDT Chandra Steele has been writing about tech for the entirety of her journalism career. She loves making tough topics easy to understand. Before joining Android Police, Chandra was senior features writer at PCMag where she did everything from interviewing Jeff Goldblum to explaining crypto. Sign in to your Android Police account Canva has helped countless people pursue their passion in graphic design with absolutely no training in it. Since its creation, there has not really been much competition when it comes to a platform that can be used by virtually anyone to create professional-looking graphics and presentations of all kinds. Google is looking to change that with Google Pics, which is both a standalone app and an integration in Google Workspace. It was announced at Google I/O 2026 back in May, but just became widely available today. How it works Google Pics, unsurprisingly, uses AI to generate images and designs. You can create new images with a prompt or you can build on pre-existing elements by uploading and modifying images from Google Drive, Photos, or your local device. While Google Pics does not offer the design freedom of Canva, where AI is optional, it has object segmentation and does allow for some tweaking so that you can edit, move, or resize specific parts of the designs it generates. As Google puts it, “no more ‘prompt-and-pray.’” Text can be translated right within the design, which lets you expand your project across multiple languages easily. How to access it You can try out Google Pics at pics.new. It’s rolling out over the next few weeks. It is available for Workspace customers with Business Standard, Business Plus, Enterprise Standard, and Enterprise Plus plans; Google AI Pro for Education users; as well as Google AI Pro and Ultra subscribers. It will be a standalone product, and also integrated with Google Drive and Slides at its start and will eventually be in Google Docs as well.","fetched_at":"2026-09-02T20:17:40.306Z","ok":true,"blocks":[{"html_en":"<p><time datetime=\"2026-09-01T19:43:28Z\"><span>Published</span> Sep 1, 2026, 3:43 PM EDT</time>\n                        </p>","sentences":[{"en":"Published Sep 1, 2026, 3:43 PM EDT","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p>Chandra Steele has been writing about tech for the entirety of <a href=\"https://authory.com/ChandraSteele\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">her journalism career</a>. She loves making tough topics easy to understand. Before joining Android Police, Chandra was senior features writer at PCMag where she did everything from interviewing Jeff Goldblum to explaining crypto.&#160; </p>","sentences":[{"en":"Chandra Steele has been writing about tech for the entirety of her journalism career.","zh":"钱德拉·斯蒂尔（Chandra Steele）在她的整个新闻职业生涯中一直在撰写有关科技的文章。"},{"en":"She loves making tough topics easy to understand.","zh":"她喜欢让困难的话题变得容易理解。"},{"en":"Before joining Android Police, Chandra was senior features writer at PCMag where she did everything from interviewing Jeff Goldblum to explaining crypto.","zh":"在加入 Android Police 之前，Chandra 是 PCMag 的高级专题撰稿人，她负责从采访 Jeff Goldblum 到解释加密货币等各种事务。"}]